 {"type":"failure","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-09-07T10:47:03.314Z","evidence":{"commit":"5bf119d04ba0e34e7822654a3dfd170fd1e4fcdd"},"description":"Cold-sandbox gate failure class (run 01M1XN2KWG6T0PHRTJWZ8R0AZX tester): fabro-server SVG render tests (get_graph_returns_svg, render_graph_from_manifest_*) spawn the real render subprocess, whose exe resolution fell back to the test binary itself when target/debug/fabro is absent. nextest on fabro-server alone never builds the CLI bin, so libtest treated __render-graph as a filter and the handler returned a 500 protocol violation. Fix: render_graph_subprocess_exe now errors clearly instead of self-spawning, and the three tests skip via render_graph_subprocess_available() when no renderer binary is resolvable; the real path still runs wherever the binary exists (fabro-cli gate builds it).","resolution":"fixed","id":"mx-d38217"}
 {"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-09-07T12:29:37.993Z","evidence":{"seeds":"fabro-56f4","commit":"31f7b88292c34d05ae38fa083d6e041b2d248212"},"name":"inline-command-output-via-output-schema","description":"Inline command-node output delivery (fabro-56f4): command.output is ALWAYS a blob ref (preview-only in preambles — a tool round-trip for prompt nodes); to deliver a command script's stdout INLINE under a dedicated context key, give the node output_schema='@schemas/<file>.schema.json' (resolved relative to the workflow dir) — the engine validates the script's JSON and stores it as output.<node_id>, a plain value that preamble_allow_keys renders whole. The key must be declared in the producing node's context_allow_keys or the preamble_allow_keys_exist lint warns. Warnings printed by such scripts must stay brace-free (engine merges stderr via 'exec 2>&1' and the validator scans for balanced JSON objects). Nu 0.115 pitfalls hit while writing gate-bounce.nu: 'str downcase' is deprecated (use 'str lowercase'); 'complete' only wraps external commands (do { cat | str join } | complete fails — capture bare 'cat' and str join its stdout); custom command signatures 'string -> string' demand piped input (use 'nothing -> string' when passing args); sd list rows may lack the labels column (use $it.labels? | default []).","files":[".fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md",".fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro"],"id":"mx-2eb2e0"}
